**The two items not fully verified here:**
- **A39 (perf gate):** median frame time is 16.7 ms and p95 is 33.3 ms, both within limits. The "no frames over 50 ms" check still fails, with 5 frames up to 76.9 ms during wafer-strip key presses and the theme switch. This is the known timing flake on this machine's software rendering; it needs a re-check on real hardware.
- **A40 (CJK locales):** the machine has no Chinese, Japanese or Korean system fonts, so those screenshots show empty glyph boxes. The layout checks pass, but whether glyphs get clipped has to be checked on a desktop OS with those fonts installed.

**What this session added:**
- **Docs:** a per-item results table in `logs/premium-acceptance.md` (screenshot and covering test for each item), and a new `logs/phase-premium-summary.md`.
- **Spec fix:** the language-menu step in `e2e/acceptance-p35.spec.ts` failed because the closing Appearance menu was still on the page. The test now waits for it to close first. The app itself was fine.
- **Focus-ring colour:** I briefly changed the colour `#201E1F` in the requirements.md amendment, then put it back. premium.md §12.1 sets the ink colour to `#201E1F`, so the previous session had it right.

